      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:43:02 GMT-0400",
      "title": "Neuroflex",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:43:26 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/section-title"
    },
    "cols2_2_3_1_3": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:44:08 GMT-0400",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:44:08 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:44:34 GMT-0400",
          "text": "<ul>\n<li>Neuroflex is the only nerve conduit indicated for the treatment of symptomatic or painful neuromas and features corrugated walls allowing it to bend up to approximately 60 degrees without forming an occlusion<sup>3,4</sup></li>\n<li>Designed to be an interface between the nerve and the sorrounding tissue to prevent the ingrowth of scar tissue</li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 23 2017 15:01:52 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured"
      }
    },
    "section_title": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:42:24 GMT-0400",
      "title": "NeuroMatrix",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:42:46 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/section-title"
    },
    "cols2_2_3_1_3_1421161483": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:47:49 GMT-0400",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:47:49 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_640047820": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:47:58 GMT-0400",
          "text": "<ul>\n<li>Use of NeuroMatrix and Neuroflex removes the risk of donor-site morbidity, scarring and neuroma formation.<sup>5,6</sup></li>\n<li>Use of a nerve conduit offers a tensionless repair option when direct suture is not possible</li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 23 2017 15:04:54 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
    "section_title_1593039448": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:42:54 GMT-0400",
      "title": "NeuroMend",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:43:13 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/section-title"
    },
    "cols2_2_3_1_3_1615196174": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:45:11 GMT-0400",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:45:11 GMT-0400",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 12:45:58 GMT-0400",
          "text": "<ul>\n<li>NeuroMend allows for a 25% overlap to potentially eliminate the need for a running suture.</li>\n<li>NeuroMend offers a self-curling design to better match the dimensions of the nerve and provides the ability to wrap nerves from 2.0mm to 12.0mm in diameter.</li>\n<li>Expected to completely resorb in about 8 months after implantation.<sup>7,8</sup><br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 23 2017 15:08:05 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
